WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier,

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.480
and welcome to Bendy and the Ink Machine.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.720
Now, when I first saw this game, it reminded me

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.080
of the old school Disney animation days

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.180
You know, back when they made

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.720
willy- steamboat willy and all that stuff um,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.280
So, it has something to do...

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.880
with old school animation

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.540
and putting ink on paper

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:29.780
*He is narrating the paper shown*

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.740
Alrighty then! I'll trust you, Joey Drew!~

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.220
I don't know what you have in store for me

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.840
Oh, That's a cute little guy

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.760
Now I don't know

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.720
if this is in any way to do with HORROR

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:39.960
at all

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.260
But it seems to have a darker fe- (trails off)

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.920
(Game voice) "-I'm here.."

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.660
"Lets see if we can find what you wanted me to see"

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:47.740
Alright~!

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.960
Man this is a weird place

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.760
The Dancing Demon

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:54.260
Ohhhhhhhhhhhh good old bendy!~

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.360
I didn't think this was a horror game when I was going in to it but holy shit-

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.380
Bendy in "SHEEP SONGS!" with Boris the Wolf

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.220
*sucks in breath*

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.720
Okay then. Hello~

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.360
What am I supposed to find here in this horrifying place of decrepitness?

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.240
Ah hi, hello. Are you a lovely projector...?

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.740
*quiet cracking and ominous music in background*

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.500
Great, that's a good sign.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.300
How you doin' Bendy? You good? Oh I'm very good.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.380
okay then

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.800
Old animation board...

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.340
Blank story boards...

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.020
Weird film reels on the walls. Don't know why those are there

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.980
Oooh what's that say..?

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.940
Dreams come truuueee

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.500
You talking about bendy coming to life?

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.200
Oh hi, how ya doin.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.740
Did Bendy come truuuee?

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.100
Ohh

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.420
That's a dark ominous hallway...

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.380
I know a dark ominous hallway when I see it!

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.720
ohhaaaohhahhhohh

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.160
Tastes like ink and blood mixed together very bad stuff

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.840
How many Bendys are here?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.020
Ooooo

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.420
Oh ink machine

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.040
Okayy

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.920
I don't know what that means or why I'm going towards it but oookaayyy

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.640
Holy fuck

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.620
(Game voice) "So this is the ink machine, huh? Wonder how you turn it on."

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.180
I don't know if that's the first thing that I'd wonder about this

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.240
I'd wonder about the horror things that's going on in here.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.840
And how it's not good at all and everyone's gonna die

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.080
Yeak ok let's turn on the horrible monstrosity that's definitely gonna kill me

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.720
ookkkaayy

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.640
wrench, do you help? weird chest-oo drawers do you help?

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.660
Oh also this is the first video that I've been able to record since we just did

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.720
a date with Markiplier and I wanted to say: Thank you guys so much for

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.460
the amazing response on that video. I'll talk about it more when i have more time

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.340
to talk about it but I just wanted to say it's been a slough and I finally took a day off

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:41.120
yesterday where I did absoutley nothing because we've been working on that no-

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:42.460
*board crashes down*

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.300
*Mark makes raspy sound*

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.960
non-stop for about a week and a half...

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.680
wwWWOAAH... Thhaat doesn't seem natural over there

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.740
I think see inky limbs and an exposed rib cage

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.700
so that's nice

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.320
ooohh hi

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:58.820
(Game voice)"Oh my God.."

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.320
yeahh

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.020
"Joey, what were you doin?"

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.960
yeah I think he's trying to make wolfie woo-

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.080
Ohhh that's horrifying

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:06.840
oohh noo

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.520
ho boy

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:10.180
okay..

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.240
that's weird.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.320
That's Borris the wolf who don't look so good.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.340
I dunno who Joey is or what Joey was doing but there's a lot of death happening here

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.460
So yeah it's kinda outta context, just thank you guys so much for the support.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.300
We worked so hard on that. We're very happy at the way it turned out

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.460
ooh boy- main power okay.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.580
(Game voice) "Alright, how do I get this to work?"

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.740
AAALLLRRIIGHHHT LET'S WHIP THIS BAD BOY INTO SHAPE I AIN'T WORRIED ABOUT

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:38.180
NOTHING GOING ON HERE THAT'S BAAADDD

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:44.600
oooohhh I thought there was a reason all those items were streewwwnnn about all over the place

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.640
*Game character gasps* "Oh..."

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.080
woooaaahh!!

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:48.020
"Who put this here?"

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.020
uhh okay, alright then.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.820
Glad you vocalized the jumpscare for me so I didn't

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:54.880
even have to think about what I was feeling.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.040
Alright

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.760
(Reading wall) Who's laughing now?

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.620
I dunno if anybody is laughing..

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.360
I'm definitely not laughing

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.760
Alright, but anyway.. just gonna go on my way

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.900
I think I know where everything was, I've seen them on the way in here

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.600
So I just gotta find em

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.420
And then somehow I've got to turn on the ink machine?

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.260
PROBABLY when I already uh-

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.020
Ok! Got THAT, that's nice!

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.860
That's real good.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:21.000
So probably I'll be able to turn on the ink machine once I get all the power up.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.780
I can't sprint so this is my MAX speed at the moment.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:25.220
But uh..

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.000
Let me just go back and get everything that I needed.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.620
*Reads wall* Dreams come true..They sure do buddy-boo!

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:31.680
They sure do!

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.380
that- oooh~ There we go I didn't even know that was a thing!

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.980
Kinda forgot was I was supposed to be getting but I got that!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:37.760
*Toy squeaks*

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.160
SQUEAAKOOO!~

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.660
Plushie doll

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:41.560
Yeesh

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:42.500
God, fuck you guys

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.500
Why are you so loud and obnoxious?

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:50.180
Uggghh.. I don't know what else I saw around here so I guess I just gotta keep exploring until I find everything.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.380
I've got THREE, which is good.. but I need more.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.100
Alright, anything over here that I-

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.860
(Game voice) "-my old desk. I wasted so much time in this chair."

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.260
WAAIT THIS DESK AT THE END OF THE HALLWAY!?

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.040
YOU'RE NOT EVEN IN YOUR OWN ROOM?!

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:04.620
YOU DON'T EVEN HAVE A WINDOW?!

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.260
okay..

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:07.820
*reading* NO.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:08.880
Alright then.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.400
Cool.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:12.500
Ohhhkaay

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.240
I'm not gonna ask many questions about it but you know what..

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.320
maybe that's for the best!

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.460
I'mma find this shit and hopefully-

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.060
*book closing sound*

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:20.780
AHA!

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.560
Got another one!

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.040
The illusion of living!

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.420
Thaaat's a weird book to read casULLy

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.140
So I've got four of six items.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.840
At least something isn't chasing me and giving me THAT trope but,

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.840
this is faaascinating here.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.120
This is weeird

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.780
I-I-I-like-I- like I love the cartoony style but also, it doesn't make a lot of sense.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.020
*recorder rattles*

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:43.940
(Tape playing voice) "At this point, I don't get what Joey's plan is for this company."

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.780
"The animations aren't sure aren't getting finished on time anymore"

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.920
"And I simply don't see why we need this...machine."

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.000
"It's noisy, it's messy, and who needs THAT much ink anyway?"

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:59.680
"Also, GET THIS, Joey had each one of us DONATE something from our workstation."

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.120
"We put them on these little pedestals in the break room"

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.740
"to help appease the GODS, Joey says, keep things going."

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.980
"I think he's lost his mind, but hey, he writes the checks."

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:14.760
"But I tell you what, if ONE MORE of these pipes burst, I'M OUTTA HERE."

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.040
*tape recorder clicks off*

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.340
OKAY! YOU KNOW, IF MY BOSS TOLD ME THAT I NEEDED TO SACRIFICE

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.400
DESK OBJECTS TO APPEASE THE GODS,

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.580
I might have a few more questions than 'If another pipe bursts'.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:27.520
Yeaaah.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:28.740
Okay then..

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.300
I guess, if you really thought about it, what could they do?

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.440
eeesh.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.360
Hello.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.840
Ahhh.. Oh, lovely.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:38.820
Oh lovely - FLOW?

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:39.840
Ink pressure?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:45.380
Ok, so I probably gotta come here last, but I still gotta find exactly what I'm looking for..

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:46.200
Ugh

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.260
I dont see anything in here that I need..

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.740
Ooooh, it automatically places them for me!

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.980
Oh that's convenient!

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.440
Okay so, I need an ink bottle, I need a cog wheel and that's it!

00:06:56.440 --> 00:07:01.400
So just an ink bottle, and a cog wheel but those should probably be on someone's desk for drawing.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.440
Maybe mine, actually.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.580
Ohp! There's a cog wheel!

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:06.980
Well grab that! So ink well must be on someone's desk,

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.720
which might be mine if I was gonna be poetic about this.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:10.480
oh

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.060
*door rattles*

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.060
why is there- OOOH

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.960
OKAY! SORRY TO DISTURB YOU!

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:16.720
I'LL CARRY OOOOON~

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:17.960
*weird dramatic sound*

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.080
OOOOH THERE IT IS! God damn, that took forever.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.820
Okay, restoring pressure which is-

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.460
(Game voice) "Okay that's all of 'em."

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.800
"Now I've just gotta get the ink flowing somehow."

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:27.480
OKAY~ I-

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.700
"There's got to be a switch around here somewhere."

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.920
*Mark talking over game, sarcastic* I WONDER WHAT SWITCH IT COULD BE?!

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:31.520
Huh.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.780
Alright then, Kerchunkles.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.360
Maybe any day now? Could I do this?

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:38.540
Is this not what I can do?

00:07:38.540 --> 00:07:40.680
Oh okay, I need to restore the ink flow.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.960
OH I KNOW WHERE THAT IS IT'S THE LONG WAY AROUND THE ONGWAY~

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.920
The way that I should have been going before but you made me sidetrack myself

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.240
so that I couldn't complete what I needed to dooo!

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.420
*Deep raspy voice* Fine.. I'll play your game

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:55.620
You ru- *gasps*

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.600
Hi, how are you doooin?

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.320
Okaay, I wasn't ready for THAT!

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.140
But I'm ready now..

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.580
OH YOU WANNA FIGHT?! HUH YOU WANNA GO?!

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:04.140
Alright, fine.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.300
*projector clicks on*

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:09.000
Hey buddy! Hey bendy! How ya doing bendy?~

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:09.880
*machine turns on with a click*

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:13.900
I don't know why the flow is all the way over here but, ya know, you have a nice day!~

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.600
You have a lovely day!

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.160
Oh hey buddy, how ya doin?

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.020
*Mark makes creeped out noise*

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.320
*banging from nearby*

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:20.980
SORRY!~

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:23.200
*unsure* Did I disturb something..?

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:23.760
*noises continue on*

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.080
Ooh, that's not good sounds.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.080
*banging gets a bit louder, closer*

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.160
Okay... AH! Sounds like somethings coming behind me

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:33.220
Thats okay! I'm not worried, it's just all the kerchunkles of all the ink flowing!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.280
I guess?

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:39.200
I don't know how this entire place is powered by pure ink but uh,

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.580
good for it!

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.220
*quietly* good for it.. good for it..

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.460
*Lever clicks, machinery hums to life, some banging noises*

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:52.180
Aaah! That's goopy! The GODS have accepted my sacrifice.. of random bullshit items!

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.900
*machinery humming loudly in background*

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.760
Ok!

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:57.280
*machinery still humming*

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.400
alright..!

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.500
So, now I guess I can turn on the ink machine..? Whatever the hell that means and whatever the hell that-

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.000
Ooooh FUC-

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:05.940
-K OFF! FUCK OFF!

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:06.900
*intense music*

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:07.680
HI?!

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.340
(Game voice) "Gotta get out of here."

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.320
OH OKAY I'LL GET OUT OF HERE THEN

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.340
ALRIGHT THEN GOODBYE!

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:13.260
*scared whimper*

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:14.900
NOW I'M SKEDADDLING!

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.360
OH NOW I'M RUNNING?!

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.140
AAAAAAAAHHHHH-

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:19.340
*higher pitch* Aaaahhh!

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:19.840
*character grunting*

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:20.340
*Mark mocking character*

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:20.840
*bang*

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:21.340
Ow!

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.620
Ow! That was a long fall!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.400
The creator LIIIEED to us.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:28.620
Ooookay

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:29.120
Alright then

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.080
I'll take this bad boy here!

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.480
(Game voice) "This will definitely come in handy."

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:38.760
Oh hell yeah, I'm sure that ink monsters are SPECIFICALLY susceptible to axes!

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.940
Can I AXE you a QUESTION?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.220
HUH?!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.800
YOU SHMELL PRETTY BAD YOU SHOULD- AXE BODY SHPRAY

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.500
*axe wooshing sound, Mark grunting*

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.660
Okay, alright then.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:50.620
Hehbleeh

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:51.180
bleeeeh

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.120
habloosky

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:52.760
bloosky~

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:53.880
habloo!

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:54.640
hablaska!

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:55.460
okay

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:56.980
Where am I now?

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:00.780
In the old animation studio..

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:01.740
*sudden door closing sound*

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:02.460
*banging*

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.500
WHAT THE FUCK?!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.220
*Banging*

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:06.740
Just gonna end it like that?!

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.300
*music begins playing*

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.680
Weeeeel Iguessthatstheend of that chapter then

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.420
Support chapter two- OH OKAY

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.940
Well that's not too bad, so that's pretty good!

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:21.440
I mean this game only cost ONE DOLLAR but that was surprisingly well made,

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:24.600
I really did enjoy it, that was not bad AT ALL!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:29.660
Um, for what it was though, in the first chapter, it's not a lot of game though,

